<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nisibis</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nisibis was a fortress city in upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, near modern Nusaybin in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, long contested between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>. Rome gained it under the treaty of 299 CE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shapur-ii">Shapur II</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> recovered Nisibis and other eastern territories in the peace of 363 CE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nisibis.jpg" alt="Nisibis" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oystercard · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Street_scene_in_Mardin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
